class_name Layouts
## Hand-made rooms, drawn as text. This is the easiest file to change yourself:
## edit a letter, and the room changes next time you play.
##
## Each room is 9 columns wide and 15 rows long. The top row is the far end, where the
## exit door is. The hero always starts at the bottom middle, so keep that clear.
##
##   .  empty floor          #  stone pillar (blocks movement and bolts)
##   b  barrel (blocks)      c  stack of crates (blocks)
##   m  skeleton minion      w  skeleton warrior
##   a  skeleton archer      g  skeleton mage
##   x  bone bomber (runs at you and explodes)
##   t  bone spitter (stays put, spits three shards)
##   s  bone spider (zig-zags, then pounces)
##   ^  spike trap (glows red, then spikes shoot up)
##   K  the boss (the Skeleton King, or the Lich on every second floor)
##
## From floor 2 a room may be mirrored left to right, and from floor 3 the far half of one
## room may be joined to the near half of another (game.gd, _twist_room), so even the
## same rooms come back different.

